  "history": {
    "en": "The Nandikeshwari temple, also called Nandikeshwari Tala, stands in the town of Sainthia in the Birbhum district of West Bengal. The present temple was built in 1913 (Bengali year 1320). Banglapedia names Nandipura among the eight famous pithas of West Bengal in the Mahapithanirupana.",
    "hi": "",
    "bn": "",
    "mr": "",
    "ta": "",
    "te": "",
    "gu": ""
  },
  "story": {
    "en": "According to the Puranas, Sati, the daughter of Daksha, gave up her life in the fire of her father's sacrifice after he insulted her husband Shiva. Grieving, Shiva carried her body across the world until Vishnu's discus divided it, and each place where a part fell became a Shakti Peetha. Tradition holds that Sati's necklace fell here.",
    "hi": "",
    "bn": "",
    "mr": "",
    "ta": "",
    "te": "",
    "gu": ""
  },
  "facts": {
    "en": [
      "Devotees tie red and yellow threads to a huge sacred banyan tree to ask for their wishes.",
      "It is one of the four famous pithas of the Birbhum district."
